        },
        "subject": "LU-21216 ldiskfs: do not normalize with empty prealloc_table",
        "message": "LU-21216 ldiskfs: do not normalize with empty prealloc_table\n\next4_mb_normalize_request() of ext4-prealloc.patch takes the goal\nwindow from s_mb_prealloc_table.  When the table is empty\n(\"echo 0 > /proc/fs/ldiskfs/<dev>/prealloc_table\"), neither window\nbranch runs: start stays 0 and size stays the file size in blocks.\nFor a write far beyond the allocated blocks of a file, the goal then\nstarts right after them and is trimmed to a group, so it need not\ncontain the request.  ext4_mb_use_inode_pa() computes a negative\nlength for it, and the OST aborts its journal:\n\n  LDISKFS-fs error (device dm-1): ldiskfs_mb_mark_diskspace_used:\n  3476: comm ll_ost_io00_005: Allocating blocks 1297408-1048576\n  which overlap fs metadata\n  Aborting journal on device dm-1-8.\n  LDISKFS-fs (dm-1): Remounting filesystem read-only\n\nKernels that align the goal to the group of the request (Linux 5.19\nand later, RHEL 8.8+ and 9.1+) instead preallocate up to a whole\ngroup for the write.\n\nKeep the original request when the table is empty, as for requests\nthat are not normalized.  Add sanity test_445.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial\nFixes: f15995b8e52b (\"LU-12335 ldiskfs: fixed size preallocation table\")\nHPE-bug-id: LUS-12766\nSigned-off-by: Andrew Perepechko <andrew.perepechko@hpe.com>\nReviewed-by: Alexey Lyashkov <alexey.lyashkov@hpe.com>\nReviewed-by: Alexander Zarochentsev <alexander.zarochentsev@hpe.com>\nAssisted-by: DSH:claude-opus-5.5\nChange-Id: I6e54608685c54bfeb825715d0248639ed87bed6c\n"
      },
